    "text": "Let's break down the problem step by step to determine how many balloons Claire has left.\n\n1. **Initial number of balloons:**\n   Claire starts with 50 balloons.\n\n2. **Balloons given to a little girl:**\n   Claire gives 1 balloon to a little girl.\n   \\[\n   50 - 1 = 49\n   \\]\n   So, after giving 1 balloon to the little girl, Claire has 49 balloons.\n\n3. **Balloons that floated away:**\n   12 balloons floated away.\n   \\[\n   49 - 12 = 37\n   \\]\n   So, after 12 balloons floated away, Claire has 37 balloons.\n\n4. **Balloons given away over the next thirty minutes:**\n   Claire gives away 9 more balloons.\n   \\[\n   37 - 9 = 28\n   \\]\n   So, after giving away 9 more balloons, Claire has 28 balloons.\n\n5. **Balloons grabbed from her coworker:**\n   Claire grabs 11 more balloons from her coworker.\n   \\[\n   28 + 11 = 39\n   \\]\n   So, after grabbing 11 more balloons, Claire has 39 balloons.\n\nTherefore, the final number of balloons Claire has is \\(\\boxed{39}\\).",
